WEBVTT

NOTE week13-clip2-thresholds
NOTE Narration read by an AI-generated voice.
NOTE The clip has its own caption along the bottom of the frame, so these cues
NOTE are placed near the top to keep the two from overlapping.

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.058 line:2 align:center
Once the model is trained, one decision
is left: where to put the threshold.

2
00:00:05.058 --> 00:00:10.959 line:2 align:center
These 2 curves are drawn to the same
height, but sepsis is only 7% of patients,

3
00:00:10.959 --> 00:00:13.092 line:2 align:center
so the red 1 is really much smaller.

4
00:00:13.092 --> 00:00:17.950 line:2 align:center
Moving the line trades missed
cases against false alarms.

5
00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:22.216 line:2 align:center
At 7% prevalence, sensitivity of 80%

6
00:00:22.216 --> 00:00:25.188 line:2 align:center
with a positive predictive value of 10%

7
00:00:25.188 --> 00:00:29.609 line:2 align:center
means 56 alerts for every 100 admissions.

8
00:00:29.609 --> 00:00:33.570 line:2 align:center
50% with 20% means 17 and a half.

9
00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:37.950 line:2 align:center
25% with 35% means 5.

10
00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:43.234 line:2 align:center
The honest unit is how many patients a
clinician reviews for each real case:

11
00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:49.840 line:2 align:center
ten, five, and about three at those three
points. The real sepsis model sat at 8,

12
00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:54.950 line:2 align:center
and it alerted on 18%
of all hospitalizations.

13
00:00:55.150 --> 00:01:00.598 line:2 align:center
None of this holds still. A lab changes
an assay, a diagnosis moves to a new code,

14
00:01:00.598 --> 00:01:05.708 line:2 align:center
a unit reopens and the case mix shifts.
None of these generates a ticket.

15
00:01:05.708 --> 00:01:11.483 line:2 align:center
The model keeps producing scores that look
plausible while the performance moves.

16
00:01:11.683 --> 00:01:15.445 line:2 align:center
So watch it. Plot the monthly
AUC against limits set

17
00:01:15.445 --> 00:01:17.977 line:2 align:center
from a period you agree was stable.

18
00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:23.364 line:2 align:center
Here it drifts below the lower limit
and stays there for three months,

19
00:01:23.364 --> 00:01:26.750 line:2 align:center
which is a signal rather than a bad month.

20
00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:31.589 line:2 align:center
Write the plan before go-live.
Track inputs, outputs and outcomes.

21
00:01:31.589 --> 00:01:36.468 line:2 align:center
Set the limits in advance. Name the
person who is paged when one is crossed,

22
00:01:36.468 --> 00:01:42.313 line:2 align:center
and decide now whether the answer is
to retrain, retune, or switch it off.
